From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shi Jiayang <shi05275@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: keep YT922x VLAN flows in software

The YT922x software tagger supplies the PVID of an access port, and an
untagged access frame does not expose that PVID to the PPE. A MAC-only
flow key would then be shared by distinct VLANs.

Keep YT922x VLAN/PPE traffic on the software path until the SoC flow key
and tag actions can represent access PVIDs. Hardware forwarding inside
the switch still uses its VLAN tables. VLAN-unaware PPE is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Shi Jiayang <shi05275@163.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
@@ -801,6 +801,20 @@ void __mtk_ppe_check_skb(struct mtk_ppe
 	int entry_len;
 	u8 *tag;
 
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NET_DSA)
+	/* An untagged access frame does not expose its bridge PVID to PPE.
+	 * Do not bind it using a MAC-only key shared by distinct VLANs.
+	 */
+	if (netdev_uses_dsa(skb->dev) &&
+	    skb->dev->dsa_ptr->tag_ops->proto == DSA_TAG_PROTO_YT922X_4B) {
+		struct dsa_port *dp;
+
+		dsa_switch_for_each_user_port(dp, skb->dev->dsa_ptr->ds)
+			if (dsa_port_is_vlan_filtering(dp))
+				return;
+	}
+#endif
+
 	spin_lock_bh(&ppe_lock);
 
 	if (FIELD_GET(MTK_FOE_IB1_STATE, hwe->ib1) == MTK_FOE_STATE_BIND)
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe_offload.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe_offload.c
@@ -211,6 +211,11 @@ mtk_flow_get_dsa_port(struct net_device
 			*push_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_standalone_vid(dp);
 		break;
 	case DSA_TAG_PROTO_YT922X_4B:
+		/* The software tagger supplies access-port PVIDs. PPE cannot
+		 * reproduce this policy yet, so retain the software path.
+		 */
+		if (dsa_port_is_vlan_filtering(dp))
+			return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 		if (!yt922x_4b_port_tag(dp->index))
 			return -ENODEV;
 		if (push_vid)
